{"game": "alien-swarm", "language": "english", "appid": 630, "month": "2016-11", "window": 1, "start_date": 1477958400, "end_date": 1478563199, "month_true_total": 142, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-06 01:01:05 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "26464854", "author": {"steamid": "76561198079704709", "personaname": "Reinhardt", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/202156/", "num_games_owned": 775, "num_reviews": 628, "playtime_forever": 6774, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4201, "last_played": 1772782033, "avatar": "7c71b081dbe0b723e40284cac46c34455ef524b8"}, "language": "english", "review": "This is one of the 1st Co-op games I've ever played on steam, and continues to be one of my favourites. It has action, thriller and teamwork all bundled up in one campaign that you must complete with 3 other players. I had good memories playing Alien Swarm with friends and others a like. Despite the repeitition of the game (there is only one campaign in the game), the outcome may differ based on your team composition, experience and other criteria. \n\nI also heard from a friend that this game was basically a F2P version of Helldivers too, lol.\n\nUnfortunately Valve no longer has updates for the game, and because of that there are many old glitches, bugs and other technical issues that hasen't been resolved by the developers. For me, the loading screen tends to stretch longer than that of my team members sometimes even leading to crashing the game.\n\nLuckily, a lot of these issues are resolved by members within the Alien Swarm community, which I would add, is fairly small now but still a nice place to relax and communicate with other members. \n\nIt's an old game, but still fun to play imo. I recommend playing it with friends, as there aren't many public matches nowadays.", "timestamp_created": 1478468004, "timestamp_updated": 1478468004, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 7, "votes_funny": 0, "weight